# QuickLabour - Platform Specifications & Architecture

This document provides a comprehensive technical overview, operational workflows, security architecture, and database schemas of the **QuickLabour** platform—a premium, on-demand marketplace connecting blue-collar trade workers (plumbers, electricians, carpenters, etc.) with clients needing local repair services in real-time.

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Core Concept

**QuickLabour** addresses the fragmentation of on-demand blue-collar labor matching by establishing a real-time marketplace. It caters to three primary roles:
1. **Clients**: Individuals who need swift, trustworthy domestic repair work completed.
2. **Workers (Labours)**: Skilled service providers seeking local job requests matching their specific trade.
3. **Administrators**: Support and operational staff who monitor transactions, moderate reviews, verify credentials, and audit system security.

> [!NOTE]
> The platform uses a hybrid matching system: once a client posts a job, the backend dynamically queries matching active workers near the location and routes bids or invitations straight to their dashboards.

